description: Gloamstead UE5 project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

This is Gloamstead, a UE5 C++/Blueprint hybrid game.

Follow docs/agents/ProjectRules.md before making architectural decisions.

Use C++ for core systems, components, interfaces, data structs, and subsystems.
Expose designer-facing fields and events to Blueprint.
Keep gameplay balance in Data Assets, Data Tables, and Curves.
Do not use GAS for MVP.
Do not add multiplayer, hunger/thirst, farming, or large procedural world systems unless explicitly requested.
Avoid backward-compatibility shims and thin wrapper layers.
Prefer direct migrations and clean implementations.

When modifying Unreal C++:
- Update headers and source files together.
- Use Unreal naming conventions.
- Keep UPROPERTY metadata practical and editor-friendly.
- Make systems Blueprint-readable where useful.
- Do not invent unrelated systems.

Before coding, identify the specific system doc being implemented.
After coding, summarize changed files and expected editor setup steps.